  m_Name: Object_9
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Turbine Housing
  description: The Turbine Housing, positioned at the middle-center-rear of the engine,
    is a medium-sized, complex, metal-bright component that surrounds and supports
    the turbine blades. Its complex shape and metal-bright material provide exceptional
    strength and durability, which are essential for withstanding the high stresses
    and temperatures generated by the turbine. Notably, the Turbine Housing's position
    at the rear of the engine allows it to work in tandem with the Exhaust Manifold
    to optimize engine efficiency.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
